{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778899134,"nonce":"44lw5RdD55f12Sbx8XODva5GoUo=","title":"Postinstall rebuild hook fails under ES modules","message":"## Problem\nThe protected-branch post-merge rebuild path runs `npm install`, which invokes `node scripts/fix-pty-permissions.js`. Because `package.json` declares `\"type\": \"module\"`, this `.js` script is executed as ESM, but it uses CommonJS `require`, failing with `ReferenceError: require is not defined in ES module scope`.\n\n## Context\nThe previous React Flow graph auth merge completed the git merge, then the rebuild hook failed at postinstall before the app could rebuild cleanly. This was visible in the completed auth request output and contributed to the rebuild splash/white page recovery path.\n\n## Proposed Fix\nConvert the postinstall helper to ESM imports and derive `__dirname` from `import.meta.url`, preserving the existing permission-fix behavior.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}